# Falling-stone at-rest cue (#360): the loose overhang, native 24x8 frames, drawn with its top on the stone's top,
# centred on the stone. loose: a cracked rock lip with the stone's crown wedged in it (at rest and through the warning);
# broken: the lip with the empty socket (from the fall on). Same rock palette as stone.grid.
